  1295                              <1> ;Bytes 0 to 20 (21 bytes): Secret DOS search data. Ignore this completely.
  1296                              <1> 
  1297                              <1> ;Byte 21 (1 byte): The File Attribute (e.g., 10h means Directory, 00h means Normal File).
  1298                              <1> 
  1299                              <1> ;Bytes 22 to 23 (2 bytes): The File Time.
  1300                              <1> 
  1301                              <1> ;Bytes 24 to 25 (2 bytes): The File Date.
  1302                              <1> 
  1303                              <1> ;Bytes 26 to 29 (4 bytes): The File Size. (The lower 16-bits are at Byte 26, the upper 16-bits are at Byte 28).
  1304                              <1> 
